{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "555689bc-dc80-8af9-ade0-afd5bb52a244",
  "created_at": "2026-01-29T10:16:59-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Linh Okafor",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:14:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:14:59-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, um, I'm calling about my water and sewer bill. I need to change the mailing address on it, and I want to go paperless, if that's, um, possible."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:09-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, we can do both. Is the new mailing address a different house, or a P.O. box?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:15-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A P.O. box. I keep missing the paper bills in the pile at the house, and honestly the last one was way too high. [pause] The toilet was running constantly last month, I didn't catch it for weeks, and now they're charging me for all of it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:30-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, that'll do it. A running toilet can put through a lot of water. Once it's fixed, the usage should drop back to normal on the next reading. If you've got a repair receipt, send it along with a note and someone can look at the bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I fixed it already. It's just, it's a lot for something that was a flapper. [line breaks up] Sorry, I'm on speaker, I've got my hands full. Can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:55-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, I hear you fine. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:15:58-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, the bill is due soon, and I'm at work all day. Is there a drop box or something? For after the office closes?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:06-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there's a drop box at City Hall for payments. Check or money order, made out to the city, and put your account number on it. Nobody needs to be there when you drop it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:17-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. I'll do that on my way home. I was gonna sell some stuff anyway, I've got this old coin collection I'm thinking of selling, so maybe that'll cover it, ha, I don't know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:28-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, hopefully. Now, for the paperless setup, I'll need your account number and the new mailing address, and an email for the e-bills."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:36-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, okay, hold on, let me find the bill. It's, uh, [inaudible] sorry, it's in the car. Can I call you back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:44-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, no problem. Ask for billing and it'll come to me or one of the others. Do you want me to note the toilet issue on your account in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:54-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, please. That'd be good. Thanks, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-29T10:16:57-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Anytime. Take care."
    }
  ],
